cast<br /> <b><u><a href=\"http://atrusilk.podbean.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://atrusilk.podbean.com/</a></u></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8769-tavelgorge","name":"TavelGorge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T08:36:37-08:00","id":817642,"title":"","content":"I'm aware of eating crow. I have my doubts that Ex3E will see physical print in 4-6 months let alone Dragonblood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4915-darkuwa","name":"Darkuwa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4915_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T08:42:19-08:00","id":817648,"title":"","content":"You may be but its a fairly weird idiom..idiom? Is that the word? Without the tag other readers would have no idea why a conversation about book release turned into one about crow kidnapping.<br /> <br /> Physical print? Do they still print books? Arent trees extinct yet?<br /> <br /> Im fairly confident that a backer pdf will be out for DBs by then. Seeing as how the 3year protracted sneeze that has been 3e was not just the solar charmset but designing the base systems and also doing design work for the majority of the other charm sets to make sure they all come from the same framework. Till then CrowNya West's life hangs in the balance","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Exalted: Princes of the Universe<br /> A Third Edition Exalted Podcast<br /> <b><u><a href=\"http://atrusilk.podbean.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://atrusilk.podbean.com/</a></u></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8769-tavelgorge","name":"TavelGorge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T08:49:45-08:00","id":817652,"title":"","content":"While I am typically the most optimistic person about Exalted releases, it should be noted that:<br /> -First is the Core Book release. We'll get fresh PDFs and it'll go up for Print on Demand. Meanwhile backer deluxe versions will begin construction.<br /> -Next is Arms of the Chosen. This book is largely written, so it'll just need a few editing passes and production. I wouldn't be surprised in Deluxe corebooks arrived sometime after this book.<br /> -Then is The Realm book, which is NOT a splat book, but talks about the empire, the houses, and satrapies<br /> -FINALLY, then comes the Dragon Blooded book, charms and all.<br /> <br /> They will not rush these books back to back, even if they're finished. They will trickle them out at LEAST 2-3 months apart, I would bet a crow dinner on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T08:55:49-08:00","id":817659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/817600-2e-where-are-all-the-dragonblood-charms?p=817652#post817652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I am typically the most optimistic person about Exalted releases, it should be noted that:<br /> -First is the Core Book release. We'll get fresh PDFs and it'll go up for Print on Demand. Meanwhile backer deluxe versions will begin construction.<br /> -Next is Arms of the Chosen. This book is largely written, so it'll just need a few editing passes and production. I wouldn't be surprised in Deluxe corebooks arrived sometime after this book.<br /> -Then is The Realm book, which is NOT a splat book, but talks about the empire, the houses, and satrapies<br /> -FINALLY, then comes the Dragon Blooded book, charms and all.<br /> <br /> They will not rush these books back to back, even if they're finished. They will trickle them out at LEAST 2-3 months apart, I would bet a crow dinner on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, i didnt realize the gear book was.coming before Realm and DB. That feels like at least a year from the E3 core going gold (once thier done fixing the book staff can go to other products and speed them along). Oh and i think theyre doing KS for some of these books for fancy editions. So thats a minimum one month delay per book if they launch them sequentially instead of in parallel.<br /> <br /> My baaaaaad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Exalted: Princes of the Universe<br /> A Third Edition Exalted Podcast<br /> <b><u><a href=\"http://atrusilk.podbean.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://atrusilk.podbean.com/</a></u></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8769-tavelgorge","name":"TavelGorge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T09:40:51-08:00","id":817698,"title":"","content":"The usable versions of Charms are in TCA and the errata.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T10:16:11-08:00","id":817726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TavelGorge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/817600-2e-where-are-all-the-dragonblood-charms?p=817659#post817659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Right, i didnt realize the gear book was.coming before Realm and DB. That feels like at least a year from the E3 core going gold (once thier done fixing the book staff can go to other products and speed them along). Oh and i think theyre doing KS for some of these books for fancy editions. So thats a minimum one month delay per book if they launch them sequentially instead of in parallel.<br /> <br /> My baaaaaad.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they might only be doing a KS for the big splatbooks, but arms has to go through layout, then realm has to be finished and go through layout, then DBs has to be finished and go through layout. Considering it took the core book over a year to be properly organized and laid out, doing three separate books that are all in their second draft only seems daunting.<br /> <br /> I'd be surprised if we got DBs this year, considering the KS and all that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T10:20:47-08:00","id":817731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/817600-2e-where-are-all-the-dragonblood-charms?p=817726#post817726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think they might only be doing a KS for the big splatbooks, but arms has to go through layout, then realm has to be finished and go through layout, then DBs has to be finished and go through layout. Considering it took the core book over a year to be properly organized and laid out, doing three separate books that are all in their second draft only seems daunting.<br /> <br /> I'd be surprised if we got DBs this year, considering the KS and all that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> While I don't think you're wrong on your release prediction, the Corebook was stated to take so long in layout because they were INVENTING what would become the base format for the edition. They have further stated that future books will take less layout time because they now have the format and they just have to apply it to the books. So while yes, layout will add time to production, I don't think the time it took for the Corebook -- the 700 page size of it notwithstanding -- is a valid measurement against other books.<br /> <br /> This opinion is based on logical conclusions of read statements, not facts. I am not a publisher, so I could be wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T10:35:43-08:00","id":817746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/817600-2e-where-are-all-the-dragonblood-charms?p=817731#post817731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> While I don't think you're wrong on your release prediction, the Corebook was stated to take so long in layout because they were INVENTING what would become the base format for the edition. They have further stated that future books will take less layout time because they now have the format and they just have to apply it to the books. So while yes, layout will add time to production, I don't think the time it took for the Corebook -- the 700 page size of it notwithstanding -- is a valid measurement against other books.<br /> <br /> This opinion is based on logical conclusions of read statements, not facts. I am not a publisher, so I could be wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't forget to adjust for that bastard Murphy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T10:40:32-08:00","id":817754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/817600-2e-where-are-all-the-dragonblood-charms?p=817731#post817731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> While I don't think you're wrong on your release prediction, the Corebook was stated to take so long in layout because they were INVENTING what would become the base format for the edition. They have further stated that future books will take less layout time because they now have the format and they just have to apply it to the books. So while yes, layout will add time to production, I don't think the time it took for the Corebook -- the 700 page size of it notwithstanding -- is a valid measurement against other books.<br /> <br /> This opinion is based on logical conclusions of read statements, not facts. I am not a publisher, so I could be wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is true, but doing three smaller projects that total a big one almost always take longer. Combine that with the fact that every aspect of exalted third edition has taken drastically longer than anyone expected, and I'm not entirely convinced that they can just polish off three books, one that big and crunch heavy as well as fluff heavy, to the point where we get the PDFs in a year.<br /> <br /> I don't think it will take too much more than a year, but the developers are busy and probably pretty burned out after finishing the core book. Or they probably will be when the core book gets finished, they've still got to do backer charms and stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T10:57:43-08:00","id":817767,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure the backer charm thing is happening right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T11:01:17-08:00","id":817772,"title":"","content":"Remember last winter? When everyone was like &quot;oh my god it's so close it's so close!&quot; And I asked Rich &quot;Hey, since we're soooo close, can you give a tiny, super tentative estimate on when it might be released? Like mid-March? Or are we talking like don't get your hopes up, it'll be like June.&quot; <br /> <br /> Hah, June. <br /> <br /> Anyway, right now the three books yet to be released aren't even in the spot that the third Ed core was this time last year. let's say Arms moves to layout in two months, that's about April. Spends maybe, another two months in layout, it might have been a bit shorter but Maria took a two week vacation because she hasn't had one in a while, and that always bleeds out past two weeks because packing, unpacking, getting settled ect. Then there's all the messing about with drivethru rpg that can take a few days, all the final passes by the devs and CCP and stuff, that'll take us at least into July.<br /> <br /> Then the realm goes to layout in July, spends about two and a half months there because everything is running smooth now, no delays. It's a big book with lots of pictures though. Then messing around with CCP final passes and all that. That brings us almost to October, and thn you need to get out the DB book in two and a half months, including a month long kickstarter.<br /> <br /> It SOUNDS silly that you couldn't get out three books in a year, but when you break it down it's not that hard to push that timetable into 2017.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}